# ---- one home for the verdict (BH-1024) ----
# The FALLBACK for the settings row `verdict_single_home`, which is where this
# knob really lives (jobs-client.sh setting-set verdict_single_home 1). Read
# only when the row is absent or the worker predates it. 1 makes the LEDGER the
# first reader in three places: bin/review-prs.sh starts writing a verdict row
# per reviewed (PR, sha), bin/review-autopilot.sh's already-reviewed skip asks
# the ledger before state/<project>.pr-reviews.json, and the merge conductor's
# autopilot-verdict consume asks it before the `apverdict` line in attempts.txt.
# 0 (the default, and the seeded row's value) is today's behaviour byte for
# byte; the files stay write-through caches either way.
#VERDICT_SINGLE_HOME=0

